2	// Entry point — CSS Cascade Layers ordering.
3	//
4	// Load order:
5	//   1. Font @imports (MUST be at stylesheet root — CSS spec forbids @import
6	//      nested inside @layer blocks; violation silently drops the rules and
7	//      breaks web fonts like Clash Display / --fm-en).
8	//   2. @layer declaration — fixes priority independent of source order.
9	//   3. Layer blocks populated via meta.load-css so each partial stays
10	//      independently editable and source maps resolve to the original file.
11	//
12	// Layer priority (low → high):
13	//   reset < base < layout < components < pages < utilities < state
14	//
15	// Rationale:
16	//   - `pages` sits above `components` so page-specific overrides win without
17	//     specificity games.
18	//   - `utilities` above `pages` so `.f-display-0`, `.--regular`, `.--fm-en`
19	//     etc. always trump page/component rules — mirrors the old @use source
20	//     order where base/ loaded before components/ and utils were always last.
21	//   - `_root.scss` (CSS custom properties + typography/color/container utility
22	//     classes) lives in `utilities` so .f-*/.clr-* classes win over components
23	//     and pages. :root{} custom properties work correctly in any layer.
24	//   - `state` is the highest — TS-driven `data-reveal`, `data-mask`, `is-*`
25	//     dynamic state always wins, without !important.
26	// =============================================================================
