### 3. **Responsive Breakpoint Patterns**

**Container Size Tokens** (in `_variables.scss`):
```scss
$containers: (
  3xl: 1920,   // max-width desktop
  2xl: 1640,
  xl: 1440,
  lg: 1024,
  md: 768,     // tablet & landscape phone
  sm: 544,     // mobile
  xs: 375,     // small mobile
);
```

**Mixin Usage:**
- `@include mq($key-or-size, $direction: "max")` — Media query helper
- `@include mq-max(key)` — `max-width` breakpoint (default, mobile-first)
- `@include mq-min(key)` — `min-width` breakpoint
- Example: `@include mq(md)` = `@media (max-width: 768px) { ... }`

**Responsive Patterns Found in Works:**

Works Canvas responsive:
```scss
@include mq(md) {
  &__bottom-controls {
    width: calc(100vw - fluid(24, 32));
    max-width: fluid(340, 420);
  }
}

@include mq(sm) {
  &__bottom-toggle {
    @include font("f-body-5");
  }
}
```

Works Detail View responsive:
```scss
&__info {
  grid-template-columns: 10fr 2fr;  // desktop

  &-list {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);  // 4 column grid
  }
}

@include mq(md) {
  &__info {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;  // single column on tablet
  }

  &__info-list {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);  // but 4-col list items
  }
}

@include mq(sm) {
  // single column for everything
}
```

**Fluid Typography System:**
- `@function fluid($min, $max, $x1: 375, $x2: 1920)` — CSS `clamp()` for responsive sizing
- `@include font("f-heading-1")` — Uses fluid typography maps
- `@include fs-fluid($min, $max)` — Direct fluid font sizing

